Hanoi, February 11, 2018 (VNA) – Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD) on the morning of February 11, 2018, during their visit to Brunei Darussalam.
University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest center of higher education and scientific research in Brunei, and ranks third in the university ranking in the region.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam-Brunei cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established a cooperative relationship with Vietnam FPT University in July 2013, and the main cooperation area is English training.
In addition to English, French, German, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei Darussalam has also included Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During the visit to the University of Brunei Darussalam, the Prime Minister of Vietnam Nguyen Tan Dung and his wife had an exchange with students of Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is happy that more and more foreigners are learning Vietnamese, and he will actively contribute to promoting the image of Vietnamese culture and local characteristics to the world.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet expressed his confidence and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will be strengthened; that students in the Vietnamese language classes will be increasingly interested in the Vietnamese language, will work hard to learn it, will be able to speak fluently Vietnamese at an early age and will become ambassadors of friendly and cooperative relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also took the opportunity to communicate with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Center in Chanh Muong District, Quang Nam Province, via video, to learn about their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, believed that the cooperation relationship between Vietnam FPT University and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, was a vivid symbol of the cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei in education.
It is hoped that the students of the Centre will make greater progress in their studies and contribute positively to the friendly and cooperative relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly appreciated the achievements of the two countries in education cooperation during his discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. These achievements include the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese language in the teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Lim Jong-hyeon hopes that the University of Brunei Darussalam will continue to pay attention to ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the scale of Vietnamese language classes.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, also highly evaluated the positive effects of cooperation between the two countries on the basis of the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively carry out various short-term exchange training projects, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha highly appreciated the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei Darussalam in Vietnam; he believed that the university would become stronger in terms of regional and world development; and he hoped to further expand cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
On this occasion, Prime Minister and his wife planted a memorial tree on the campus of the University of Brunei and left a message in the memorial book.
Prime Minister Lim has wished that the University of Brunei Darussalam will continue to develop and contribute more power to the education industry of Brunei, and develop deeper and broader cooperation with Vietnam's educational and training institutions.
(continued)
Vietnam News Agency
"Important engine of global recovery"-China News Network
"China’s economy demonstrated strong resilience in responding to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic."
Recent market expectations indicate that the international community is generally positive about China’s future development.
Julio Ríos, a renowned Spanish expert on China and honorary advisor to the China Policy Observatory Network, said in an interview with the newspaper that China's current epidemic prevention and control has entered a new phase, and the dynamics of economic and social development will be further unleashed.
Liuos said that in the face of various unexpected factors, China has calmly dealt with them with its outstanding economic governance experience and measures, which fully reflects its economic resilience and management level.
China is firmly committed to expanding its openness to the world, and the internal driving force of economic development is increasing, with State-owned enterprises and private enterprises developing in synergy.
The two-year national conferences are held every year in China, where delegates discuss the overall development of the country and hot issues of the people &apos; s lives, and where broad consensus is reached, people &apos; s hearts are united and wisdom is gathered, thus contributing to China &apos; s development.
“Since the reform and opening up, China has achieved long-term high-speed development, and has now entered the stage of high-quality development.
The international community is looking forward to China &apos; s wisdom and China &apos; s programme, and to China &apos; s development bringing new opportunities to the world.
"Li said that China is currently making every effort to promote scientific and technological innovation, inject new impetus into economic and social development, and "investment, talent training, and policy incentives have made China continue to be full of vitality in the new five-year plan,"" he said.
In Rio’s view, economic institutional reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Chinese Communist Party, China has taken active measures to stabilize its economy, using both the strengths of the market economy and the superiority of the socialist system.
Focusing on expanding domestic demand as its strategic base, China will increase financial support for real economy development and encourage innovation to promote employment and raise living standards of the Chinese people. It will also meet their diverse needs for consumption at multiple levels. In this way, China will fully implement new development concepts in an accurate and comprehensive manner, striving for high-quality development and building a new pattern of development that benefits the world. This will bring more growth opportunities to the world.
This year is the 10th anniversary of the proposal of the Belt and Road Initiative.
“Economic stabilization and recovery after the pandemic is the common goal of the international community.
China's economic development potential will continue to be released, bringing more benefits to the world, and becoming an important engine for global recovery.
"Rios said that he looked forward to continuing to build the cooperation of the "Belt and Road" to play an important role in improving the level of infrastructure of various countries and strengthening mutual connection in various fields, and to continue to release more energy.
